#Lua SEXPs

$Operator: absolute-key-pressed
$Category: Status
$Subcategory: LUA-Condition
$Minimum Arguments: 1
$Maximum Arguments: 1
$Return Type: Boolean
$Description: Checks to see if the specified key was pressed. Returns true if the key was pressed, false otherwise. This sexp differs from the normal 'key-pressed' sexp because it does not care about key binding changes, and simply checks if the specified key was pressed. Use in conjunction with 'absolute-key-reset'. Note, does not work in multiplayer.
$Parameter: 
	+Description: Name of key to check, as string. For example, '1' without the quotes.
	+Type: String

$Operator: absolute-key-reset
$Category: Change
$Subcategory: LUA-Action
$Minimum Arguments: 1
; No maximum arguments means that it accepts a variable number of arguments
$Return Type: Nothing
$Description: Resets the specified key. This sexp differs from the normal 'key-reset' sexp because it does not care about key binding changes, and simply resets the actual key specified. Use in conjunction with 'absolute-key-pressed'. Note, does not work in multiplayer.   
$Repeat
$Parameter: 
	+Description: Name of key to reset, as string. For example, '1' without the quotes.
	+Type: String

#End